    "slug": "storypole-update-file-reports-success-but-leaves-target-files-unchanged-c03e86",
    "title": "storypole update stored a comma-separated list argument as one bogus value",
    "description": "The filed symptom did not reproduce: `--file <one path>` stores that path correctly, and the handler has been correct since it was introduced (73e38dd - the only commit that ever touched it).\n\nWhat does reproduce is the shape most people type: `--file a.rs,b.rs`, which stored the single string \"a.rs,b.rs\" and reported success. The scope then held one path that exists nowhere, which is indistinguishable from the update being ignored and is a plausible origin for the report.\n\nFixed by giving all four list arguments `value_delimiter = 0x2C` - file, symbol, label, criterion - since the defect is in list parsing rather than in one field. Repeating the flag still works.",
    "kind": "bug",
